.git-backup-filter-repo/

# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Generated documentation exports (regenerable via scripts/export_docs.sh) — §11.4.30
_exports/
docs/**/_exports/
.git-backups/
/server/loadtest
/server/ota-device-emu

# Tier-1 container E2E build artifacts + staging dirs (regenerable via
# tests/emulator/tier1_container_e2e.sh) — §11.4.30 no-versioned-build-artifacts
/bin/
/server/.docker-bin/
/tests/emulator/.docker-bin/
.helixqa_selftest.*/
# Runtime stress/chaos evidence (resilience_test.go) — the committed reference is
# docs/qa/20260608-stress-chaos/; re-runs write here so they never dirty the tree.
/docs/qa/stress-chaos-runs/
# Scratch validation-run output (overnight sweep logs, ad-hoc test transcripts).
# Committed evidence lives under docs/qa/<run-id>/; this dir is pure scratch and
# MUST NOT dirty the tree (§11.4.30 / §11.4.121). 0 tracked files at introduction.
/qa-results/
# RK3588 A/B-virt emulator (PWU-AB-*) guest-image build output — regenerable via
# tests/emulator/ab_virt/build_image.sh (§11.4.77 regen mechanism). Large, never versioned.
/tests/emulator/ab_virt/out/
/tests/emulator/ab_virt/.buildroot-dl/

# Docs Chain (§11.4.106) — temporary state files, never versioned
.docs_chain/state/*.tmp
.docs_chain/*.tmp
# docs_chain is a registered git submodule -- do NOT ignore (§11.4.106 OTA-014)
node_modules/
src-tauri/gen/
src-tauri/icons/
src-tauri/icons-source/
src-tauri/Cargo.lock
src-tauri/target/
playwright-report/
test-results/
package-lock.json
# SQLite WAL/shm sidecars (§11.4.95) — transient, regenerable from tracked .db
docs/workable_items.db-shm
docs/workable_items.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Playwright UI test screenshots — regenerable runtime artifacts (§11.4.30 / §11.4.77)
tests/helixqa/screenshots/
# package.json is a Node.js/Playwright dependency manifest — keep gitignored;
# the package-lock.json sibling is already gitignored above (§11.4.30 build-derivative).
package.json

# HelixTrack — space runtime data (regenerable via onboarding wizard) — §11.4.77
# data/ dirs contain per-space database + logs (regenerable); config.json is tracked.
/helix_track/spaces/*/data/

# Transient stress/chaos test outputs (any depth) — §11.4.30/§11.4.128, regenerated on run
qa-results/

# §11.4.30 — helixqa_runner build artifact + transient report (regenerable via go build + run)
tools/helixqa_runner/helixqa_runner
tools/helixqa_runner/orchestrator_report.json

# Superpowers SDD session-local scratch/ledger (§11.4.30 — never versioned)
.superpowers/
